            <ArticleTitle>Quadrilateral space syndrome: a rare cause of shoulder pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>797-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The authors report a case of quadrilateral space syndrome in a baseball pitcher. The diagnosis was made by means of subclavian arteriography performed with the arm in abduction and external rotation. This entity is a rare cause of shoulder pain caused by occlusion of the posterior humeral circumflex artery in the quadrilateral space.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
